WEBVTT

00:02.606 --> 00:04.976
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:05.043 --> 00:08.216
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:08.316 --> 00:11.891
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:11.957 --> 00:14.896
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:14.996 --> 00:18.303
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:18.369 --> 00:21.710
♪ Lucky there's a man who
positively can do ♪

00:21.843 --> 00:23.213
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:23.279 --> 00:24.516
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:24.649 --> 00:30.460
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy. ♪

00:36.807 --> 00:38.409
[sighs] Son of a bitch.

00:38.544 --> 00:39.513
What's wrong, Peter?

00:39.579 --> 00:41.517
Eh, our I.T. guy told me today
that, apparently,

00:41.584 --> 00:44.523
I've had a work e-mail address
ever since I started there.

00:44.590 --> 00:47.596
So now I got to slog
through 17,000 messages.

00:47.663 --> 00:50.400
Aw, crap, we didn't have
to come in on 9/11?

00:50.467 --> 00:52.973
I never even liked working
at that stupid brewery.

00:53.073 --> 00:55.377
Hardly my dream job,
I'll tell you that much.

00:55.444 --> 00:57.716
Now, there's
an interesting question.

00:57.816 --> 00:59.619
What would be your dream job?

00:59.719 --> 01:01.591
Dream job? Oh, that's easy.

01:01.657 --> 01:02.693
Ever since I was a kid,

01:02.793 --> 01:06.198
I always pictured myself
being an international spy.

01:09.907 --> 01:12.144
♪ ♪

01:13.147 --> 01:15.985
So, beautiful,
which lamp did you unplug

01:16.019 --> 01:17.756
to charge your phone
in the room?

01:17.822 --> 01:19.125
Mine's in the bathroom.

01:19.225 --> 01:21.864
Mm, you know,
I never caught your name.

01:21.897 --> 01:25.739
The name is Band. Lap Band.

01:25.805 --> 01:27.341
-[rapid gunfire]
-[screams]

01:28.611 --> 01:31.249
Careful. Here come the bad guys
from whatever country

01:31.316 --> 01:33.755
won't offend American
or Chinese audiences.

01:33.821 --> 01:35.558
-[gunfire]
-[grunts]

01:35.624 --> 01:38.564
You have dishonored the people
of Finland, Mr. Band.

01:38.631 --> 01:41.168
Shoot him,
fellow tall introverts.

01:43.340 --> 01:46.178
["Bond 77" by Marvin Hamlisch
playing]

01:58.003 --> 02:00.207
Yep. All definitely me.

02:00.307 --> 02:02.044
Whoosh. Zoom.

02:02.111 --> 02:04.716
Ski noise.

02:13.032 --> 02:16.774
[to tune of Pilot's "Magic"]
♪ Oh, oh, Ozempic... ♪

02:16.874 --> 02:18.309
They threw a ton of money at us.

02:18.376 --> 02:19.746
We couldn't say no.

02:19.813 --> 02:22.852
[dramatic, jazzy theme playing]

02:30.635 --> 02:32.337
[Peter chuckling]
All right.

02:32.404 --> 02:34.976
Hey, I wonder who they got
to do the song.

02:35.076 --> 02:36.980
Blech.

02:37.047 --> 02:39.853
♪ When you're a spy ♪

02:39.919 --> 02:43.093
♪ You got a lot on your mind ♪

02:43.193 --> 02:46.098
♪ You look high and low ♪

02:46.165 --> 02:50.073
♪ You never know
what you'll find ♪

02:50.207 --> 02:52.679
♪ Spy life. ♪

02:53.446 --> 02:56.252
[Peter sighs]
Mercifully brief.

03:00.094 --> 03:01.630
Good morning, Agent 5-5-5.

03:01.730 --> 03:04.869
Ugh, right. 'Cause this is
a number on a television show.

03:04.936 --> 03:08.276
I say, you look as bewitching
as ever, Miss Takeapenny.

03:08.343 --> 03:10.648
Oh, didn't you hear?
I got married.

03:10.715 --> 03:12.819
I'm now
Ms. Takeapenny-Leaveapenny.

03:12.885 --> 03:14.622
Wow, lucky gentleman.

03:14.689 --> 03:16.994
Because he gets to plow you,
is what I mean.

03:17.060 --> 03:18.531
So debonair.

03:18.597 --> 03:21.135
You know, now that I'm married,
I'm actually leaving.

03:21.202 --> 03:23.640
I'm training
my replacement, Todd.

03:23.741 --> 03:25.143
A male secretary?

03:25.243 --> 03:27.649
[sighs] Well, I suppose
I'll just have to adapt

03:27.749 --> 03:28.851
and harass him now.

03:28.952 --> 03:30.889
Nice penis, Todd.

03:30.989 --> 03:32.258
Oh, Mr. Band.

03:32.324 --> 03:34.028
Okay, good,
he knows how to play along.

03:34.128 --> 03:35.799
Yeah, this is-- this'll work.

03:35.899 --> 03:38.605
I understand you have
a mission for me, M,

03:38.671 --> 03:41.543
which I can only assume
stands for "man."

03:42.879 --> 03:44.382
Good morning, Mr. Band.

03:44.449 --> 03:46.820
Whoa. My boss is
the new Little Mermaid

03:46.887 --> 03:48.056
I'm so mad about.

03:48.123 --> 03:50.728
Mr. Band, we have
reports of a plan

03:50.828 --> 03:53.166
to intercept a European
nuclear device

03:53.232 --> 03:56.139
by the villainous
mastermind, Blofella.

03:56.172 --> 03:57.441
Got it, M.

03:57.575 --> 04:01.917
Or-or is it maybe MHM
and you pronounce it "mm-hmm"?

04:02.017 --> 04:03.252
M is fine.

04:03.319 --> 04:05.156
Okay, yeah, I--
times have changed

04:05.223 --> 04:06.893
and I-I got to--
I need to catch up.

04:08.029 --> 04:10.266
♪ ♪

04:14.576 --> 04:17.347
Oh, hey, Q.
Hey, have you seen who M is?

04:17.447 --> 04:19.218
Which I totally support,
by the way.

04:19.318 --> 04:21.189
In fact, it was my idea
and I fought for it.

04:21.255 --> 04:22.291
You should've heard me.

04:22.391 --> 04:24.328
Okay, just let me show you
the cutting-edge equipment

04:24.395 --> 04:25.932
you'll need for your mission.

04:26.032 --> 04:29.572
First, I have this fridge
that displays today's headlines.

04:29.639 --> 04:32.078
Did-- did you just go
to Best Buy?

04:32.178 --> 04:34.348
No. I also have these headphones

04:34.448 --> 04:36.452
that block out
ambient plane noise.

04:36.553 --> 04:38.155
Yeah, you-you just went
to Best Buy.

04:38.222 --> 04:40.762
-I did not!
-So, where am I headed?

04:40.828 --> 04:41.830
We're expecting Blofella

04:41.864 --> 04:44.035
to attempt to intercept
the bomb in Belgium.

04:44.101 --> 04:45.204
Oh, awesome.

04:45.304 --> 04:46.640
That's the country where
they basically have

04:46.707 --> 04:47.876
dessert for breakfast, right?

04:47.942 --> 04:50.848
Agent triple-five,
I cannot stress enough--

04:50.915 --> 04:53.019
no dessert for breakfast.

04:54.021 --> 04:56.058
♪ ♪

05:03.407 --> 05:05.209
Greetings, Mr. Band,

05:05.276 --> 05:07.615
on behalf of Belgian
Secret Services.

05:07.715 --> 05:09.352
Oh, hey.
I-I'd shake your hand,

05:09.418 --> 05:11.624
but my arm is syrup-glued
to the table.

05:11.724 --> 05:14.563
The name is Alice. Alice Boobs.

05:14.630 --> 05:17.468
[giggles]
That works in two ways.

05:17.536 --> 05:19.940
No, it's-it's really just one.

05:20.006 --> 05:22.043
♪ ♪

05:23.212 --> 05:26.820
Our intelligence has revealed
that the bomb transfer is

05:26.853 --> 05:31.096
to take place in this warehouse
for generic wooden crates.

05:31.162 --> 05:34.001
♪ ♪

05:38.510 --> 05:41.282
-[helicopter whirring loudly]
-[speaking indistinctly]

05:41.382 --> 05:43.220
What? It's very loud.

05:43.286 --> 05:45.524
[shouting indistinctly]

05:47.729 --> 05:49.398
We're getting none of this.

05:49.431 --> 05:50.835
If we can't hear him,

05:50.901 --> 05:53.373
he can't hear us saying
we can't hear him.

05:53.439 --> 05:54.876
What a mess!

05:55.010 --> 05:56.312
Gavin. Gavin.

05:56.412 --> 05:58.216
Turn off--
turn the helicopter off.

05:58.283 --> 06:02.157
I-I was going to say, "Sorry
to drop in on your party,"

06:02.257 --> 06:04.061
but, uh, feels stupid now.

06:04.128 --> 06:05.297
Get 'em, boys.

06:05.363 --> 06:06.866
So that's it, Blofella?

06:06.933 --> 06:08.738
You're just gonna have us
killed by your henchmen?

06:08.804 --> 06:11.142
Oh, okay, I'd rather you
not use that word.

06:11.209 --> 06:13.145
They are independent
contractors.

06:13.246 --> 06:14.750
He doesn't want
to pay us benefits.

06:14.816 --> 06:17.455
There is an app they log into
when they want to work,

06:17.522 --> 06:19.391
around their schedule.

06:19.458 --> 06:23.033
I am not their employer.
The app is their employer.

06:23.100 --> 06:24.903
Goodbye, Mr. Band.

06:25.003 --> 06:27.040
[laughing maniacally]

06:28.009 --> 06:30.079
[grunting]

06:37.728 --> 06:38.798
[groans]

06:38.898 --> 06:40.801
[Peter]
It wasn't looking good.

06:40.901 --> 06:43.472
But thankfully,
Q had supplied me with...

06:44.709 --> 06:46.847
Captain America's shield.

06:46.880 --> 06:48.183
[Quagmire]
What? No, no, no.

06:48.249 --> 06:49.084
You can't just become

06:49.151 --> 06:50.821
a Marvel character
halfway through.

06:50.888 --> 06:53.193
[Joe]
Also, we usually see
all the stuff

06:53.293 --> 06:54.629
Q gives you at the beginning.

06:54.729 --> 06:57.167
This feels very unearned.

06:57.233 --> 07:00.140
[Peter]
Belgian intelligence learned
that Blofella's plan was

07:00.206 --> 07:02.377
to use the nuclear device
he'd intercepted

07:02.477 --> 07:05.016
to blow up the city
of Las Vegas.

07:05.083 --> 07:07.387
But that wasn't the only
emergency I was dealing with.

07:07.487 --> 07:10.059
Yeah, you said everyone
in Vegas wears tuxedos,

07:10.126 --> 07:12.632
and I'm starting to feel
pretty self-conscious.

07:12.732 --> 07:14.502
Uh, I didn't say "definitely."

07:14.569 --> 07:16.606
I said,
"It was my understanding."

07:16.706 --> 07:19.478
[gasps]
Agent triple-five, look.

07:20.380 --> 07:21.716
[cheering]

07:21.783 --> 07:25.524
[gasps]
Blofella. Not on my watch.

07:28.229 --> 07:29.532
-[grunts]
-[screams]

07:32.070 --> 07:33.674
[slot machine chiming]

07:38.618 --> 07:40.521
[exhausted panting]

07:40.621 --> 07:42.525
I can't find my way out.

07:42.592 --> 07:45.464
Okay, well, that says
"breakfast buffet" that way,

07:45.531 --> 07:47.468
but I'm pretty sure
we've seen it twice.

07:47.535 --> 07:49.706
♪ ♪

07:51.042 --> 07:53.446
Here we are again
at North Suite Elevators.

07:53.514 --> 07:54.983
I don't know, should we--
should we just

07:55.049 --> 07:56.620
hit the slot machines
while we're here?

07:56.686 --> 07:58.256
No. That's why they do this.

07:58.323 --> 07:59.492
No, no, yeah, no,
I get all that,

07:59.560 --> 08:01.763
and I hate
to hold things up, but...

08:01.830 --> 08:03.700
I mean, Santana's in his 70s.

08:03.800 --> 08:06.238
We should probably see him
while we still can.

08:06.305 --> 08:07.508
Eh.

08:07.608 --> 08:10.548
[guitar solo playing]

08:10.615 --> 08:12.551
[Peter]
I knew one song.

08:12.652 --> 08:14.355
[guitar solo ends]

08:14.455 --> 08:15.758
Son of a bitch.

08:15.858 --> 08:18.229
♪ ♪

08:21.770 --> 08:23.774
There we are. Assembly complete.

08:23.874 --> 08:25.912
So, again, this would be
an appropriate time

08:26.012 --> 08:28.282
for you all to please
log out of the app.

08:28.349 --> 08:30.921
-[Band] Ha! I got you now.
-[gasps]

08:32.324 --> 08:33.961
Mr. Band.
How did you find me?

08:34.061 --> 08:36.967
Honestly, I'm on a guided tour
for the movie The Hangover,

08:37.067 --> 08:38.202
which ends on the roof.

08:38.269 --> 08:41.075
Fun fact, gang--
it was actually Zach's idea

08:41.108 --> 08:43.680
to put the sunglasses
on the baby.

08:43.747 --> 08:46.018
Okay, I see everyone staring
at the Mandalay Bay,

08:46.085 --> 08:49.158
so I'll go ahead and tell you
which window was the shooter's.

08:49.224 --> 08:50.327
Well, you're too late.

08:50.427 --> 08:52.598
In a few moments,
all of Las Vegas will be

08:52.665 --> 08:54.068
totally wiped off the map.

08:54.168 --> 08:55.671
[grunting]

08:55.738 --> 08:58.076
You're a madman.
Why are you doing this?

08:58.209 --> 09:00.981
I need to get out of a very
restrictive time-share deal,

09:01.081 --> 09:03.788
and this is literally
the only way out.

09:03.854 --> 09:05.858
♪ ♪

09:11.335 --> 09:12.772
[Peter]
There was no time.

09:12.838 --> 09:15.578
So that's when I pulled out
Kylo Ren's lightsaber

09:15.645 --> 09:17.414
and knocked Blofella
off the roof.

09:17.481 --> 09:18.650
[screams]

09:18.717 --> 09:19.886
[Quagmire]
No, no, no, no. That's cheating.

09:19.953 --> 09:21.455
[Joe]
Also, you got a lightsaber,

09:21.557 --> 09:23.393
and you're just gonna
push a guy?

09:23.459 --> 09:24.529
[thud]

09:24.596 --> 09:27.835
Oh, triple-five,
you saved my life.

09:27.902 --> 09:29.939
Make love to me right now.

09:29.973 --> 09:33.179
I'm sorry, Alice, I can't.
I'm gay.

09:33.279 --> 09:35.818
New Bond. Edited for snowflakes.

09:41.262 --> 09:43.166
♪ ♪

09:43.233 --> 09:45.738
Wow, that was awesome hearing
about your dream job, Peter.

09:45.804 --> 09:48.877
But I was actually lucky enough
to have my dream job.

09:48.977 --> 09:50.280
At least until I lost it.

09:50.380 --> 09:52.618
It all started years ago.

09:52.685 --> 09:55.156
It was the 1980s,
and I was living alone

09:55.223 --> 09:57.929
in a studio apartment
with an askew poster

09:57.996 --> 10:00.399
because bachelors never hang
their posters straight.

10:00.500 --> 10:01.837
[Peter]
Yeah, no offense, Quagmire,

10:01.937 --> 10:03.005
but I'm gonna listen
to this story

10:03.072 --> 10:05.143
the same way I do
most podcasts--

10:05.243 --> 10:07.080
at 1.5 speed.

10:07.147 --> 10:08.717
[Quagmire, sped up]
I'd put on some weight

10:08.784 --> 10:10.353
from being in an abusive
relationship with a woman--

10:10.420 --> 10:12.023
-Mama Celeste.
-Abbondanza.

10:12.090 --> 10:13.861
[Peter]
All right, okay.
Ba-Back to normal speed.

10:13.927 --> 10:15.597
I-I'm in. I'm hooked.

10:16.666 --> 10:18.737
[Quagmire]
The other thing about
living in the '80s is that,

10:18.804 --> 10:20.874
wherever you went,
the actual Pointer Sisters

10:20.941 --> 10:22.779
would follow you around,
singing.

10:22.846 --> 10:24.749
[tune of "Jump (for My Love)"]
♪ Glenn ♪

10:24.815 --> 10:27.054
♪ You know this man
just mailed a bill ♪

10:27.121 --> 10:28.256
♪ To Sprint ♪

10:28.389 --> 10:29.659
♪ It's for his phone ♪

10:29.692 --> 10:31.395
♪ A landline phone. ♪

10:32.164 --> 10:33.934
[Quagmire]
I knew I needed
to get in shape,

10:34.068 --> 10:36.405
but the only forms of exercise
in the '80s were

10:36.471 --> 10:38.076
roller-skating on a dance floor

10:38.142 --> 10:41.282
or lugging around your dead boss
to use his vacation home.

10:42.217 --> 10:44.254
Back then, there were
two things I liked:

10:44.321 --> 10:45.625
gyrating my pelvis

10:45.691 --> 10:47.093
and putting vowels
next to each other

10:47.160 --> 10:48.798
that weren't normally
next to each other.

10:48.864 --> 10:50.200
I combined those two loves

10:50.300 --> 10:52.672
to create something called
"aerobics."

10:52.739 --> 10:53.840
Welcome aboard.

10:53.907 --> 10:55.744
Here's your
complimentary headband,

10:55.844 --> 10:58.750
two wristbands, waistband,
thigh band, another headband.

10:58.850 --> 11:00.420
There were a lot of bands.

11:00.521 --> 11:02.825
[Peter]
Yeah, my finger's hovering
over that 1.5 button.

11:02.926 --> 11:04.261
[Quagmire]
Yeah, okay, okay, okay.

11:04.361 --> 11:06.800
So I started teaching classes
that same week.

11:06.866 --> 11:08.637
I even created an advanced class

11:08.704 --> 11:10.774
based on how your body moves
during sex.

11:10.841 --> 11:12.879
I called it "Sexercise."

11:12.945 --> 11:15.049
♪ ♪

11:18.924 --> 11:20.828
And things took off immediately

11:20.928 --> 11:24.167
because I gave 1980s women
exactly what they wanted:

11:24.234 --> 11:26.005
long, flat butts.

11:26.105 --> 11:28.443
Come on, ladies.
Longer! Flatter!

11:28.544 --> 11:30.379
My workout program was a hit,

11:30.446 --> 11:32.985
and soon I was ready
to take it national.

11:33.052 --> 11:34.488
I was lucky enough
to get the chance to announce

11:34.556 --> 11:36.893
the filming of my video on
The Tonight Show with Johnny.

11:36.994 --> 11:39.164
[Joe]
Wow! You met Johnny Carson?

11:39.265 --> 11:41.636
[Quagmire]
Actually, that particular night
there was a guest host,

11:41.703 --> 11:43.874
John Davidson,
star of That's Incredible!

11:43.974 --> 11:46.011
So, you know, different Johnny
but still Johnny.

11:46.111 --> 11:48.551
[Peter]
No one has ever called
John Davidson "Johnny."

11:48.651 --> 11:51.455
[Quagmire]
He guest-hosted 87 times.
That's not nothing.

11:51.522 --> 11:53.994
Anyway, the night's first guest
was Jane Fonda,

11:54.094 --> 11:55.764
who was promoting 9 to 5,

11:55.864 --> 11:58.503
by far the blousiest movie
of the 1980s.

11:58.570 --> 12:00.240
So, Glenn Quagmire.

12:00.306 --> 12:01.208
It says here you created

12:01.308 --> 12:03.914
an exercise craze
called "aerobics."

12:04.014 --> 12:07.086
-What inspired that?
-Well, John... ny,

12:07.186 --> 12:09.925
one day as I did jumping jacks
alone in my apartment,

12:09.992 --> 12:12.464
I thought, "How can I take
the worst parts of this

12:12.532 --> 12:13.900
"and put it in a public setting?

12:13.967 --> 12:16.840
Plus a wall of mirrors
and street-facing windows."

12:16.907 --> 12:18.710
The interview seemed
to go great.

12:18.777 --> 12:20.079
But the next day,

12:20.146 --> 12:23.419
I realized how truly ruthless
Jane Fonda was.

12:23.520 --> 12:26.124
♪ ♪

12:26.993 --> 12:30.668
Now, Mr. Quagmire, an important
part of releasing a 1980s video

12:30.735 --> 12:34.008
is the incredibly depressing
production logo it opens with.

12:34.108 --> 12:35.844
I have a few here
to choose from.

12:35.911 --> 12:38.082
First is some vibrating
rainbow text

12:38.182 --> 12:40.420
that never quite comes
into focus.

12:40.487 --> 12:42.524
[ominous synth music playing]

12:44.261 --> 12:45.229
Uh-huh, love that.

12:45.296 --> 12:47.702
This one is just a large
bouncing "V"

12:47.802 --> 12:49.806
with an ominous keyboard noise.

12:49.873 --> 12:52.110
[ominous synth music playing]

12:54.247 --> 12:55.083
Also excellent.

12:55.183 --> 12:57.287
Or here's three capital letters

12:57.354 --> 13:00.259
all spelled with one thick,
continuous line

13:00.359 --> 13:02.030
atop a digital horizon.

13:02.097 --> 13:04.334
[ominous synth music playing]

13:06.338 --> 13:08.977
Wow, you can't miss.
Let's go with all three.

13:09.779 --> 13:11.716
Wait a minute.
What's-what's going on?

13:11.783 --> 13:12.919
Where are my leg warmers?

13:12.985 --> 13:14.822
Back then,
leg warmers were essential

13:14.922 --> 13:16.392
because that was, by far,

13:16.459 --> 13:18.530
the coldest decade
from the knee down.

13:18.597 --> 13:20.266
Did someone take my leg warmers?

13:20.333 --> 13:24.174
In place of my leg warmers,
I found only a single note.

13:27.047 --> 13:27.982
At first, I assumed

13:28.049 --> 13:30.120
Jodie Foster had stolen
my leg warmers,

13:30.186 --> 13:32.357
and I was about to go
take it out on the president.

13:32.424 --> 13:35.196
But then I realized it could
only have been one person intent

13:35.263 --> 13:39.104
on sabotaging me-- Jane Fonda.

13:39.171 --> 13:41.677
I tried my best to soldier on.

13:41.743 --> 13:42.745
Okay, don't look at my legs.

13:42.812 --> 13:45.417
And one, and two...
My calves are tiny and cold.

13:45.483 --> 13:46.786
And three, and four...

13:46.886 --> 13:48.524
But I knew, even in the moment,

13:48.624 --> 13:50.326
it was gonna be a disaster.

13:50.393 --> 13:52.196
[gasping]

13:59.746 --> 14:02.150
I never stood a chance.

14:02.250 --> 14:04.287
♪ ♪

14:06.158 --> 14:07.995
[Jane Fonda]
Hello, Glenn.

14:08.062 --> 14:11.001
Sorry you failed, but...
[chuckles] like they say,

14:11.068 --> 14:13.038
all's fair in love and aerobics.

14:13.138 --> 14:15.042
Who? Who says that? Nobody.

14:15.142 --> 14:17.648
God, now I get why everyone's
racist uncle hates you.

14:17.714 --> 14:21.054
Well, it's been nice chatting,
but if you'll excuse me,

14:21.088 --> 14:22.791
I have to go lobby our nation

14:22.891 --> 14:24.696
about cleaning up the mess
we made in Vietnam.

14:24.763 --> 14:26.967
-[audio speeds up]
-[Peter] Sorry, I went ahead
and hit the eight-X.

14:27.034 --> 14:30.206
[Quagmire]
No, you-you-you did the,
you did the right thing, Peter.

14:30.306 --> 14:32.544
[ominous synth music playing]

14:42.798 --> 14:44.902
♪ ♪

14:45.036 --> 14:47.106
Well, as far as dream jobs go,

14:47.206 --> 14:50.313
mine's always been to do
what you do, Joe, to be a cop.

14:50.413 --> 14:52.484
But, you know, one day
short of retirement,

14:52.585 --> 14:54.722
since y'all got
such a nice benefits package.

14:54.789 --> 14:59.064
Huh. Well, my dream job is to
do pretty much what I do now

14:59.131 --> 15:01.101
but be, like,
a loose cannon type cop

15:01.168 --> 15:03.039
who doesn't care
whether he lives or dies

15:03.105 --> 15:04.842
but can definitely walk.

15:04.942 --> 15:07.146
♪ ♪

15:09.117 --> 15:10.921
[Cleveland]
It was my last day on the job,

15:10.988 --> 15:13.493
and I'd just taken
my last office dump

15:13.560 --> 15:14.962
when I was called
into the chief's office.

15:15.063 --> 15:17.668
Morning, sir.
You wanted to see me?

15:17.735 --> 15:18.938
That's right.
We've been tracking

15:19.004 --> 15:20.440
a notorious drug cartel

15:20.507 --> 15:22.611
that's been bringing
tons of cocaine into L.A.

15:22.678 --> 15:26.452
Yes, cocaine has been ravaging
the Black community for years.

15:26.520 --> 15:29.057
Yeah, well, some white girl
got a minor nosebleed,

15:29.123 --> 15:31.428
so now I guess it's, like,
a big frickin' deal.

15:31.495 --> 15:33.767
In fact, last night,
there was a huge bust.

15:33.833 --> 15:35.269
Wow, how much was it?

15:35.336 --> 15:37.207
And remember,
we measure cocaine--

15:37.274 --> 15:39.812
and nothing else--
in only kilos.

15:39.879 --> 15:42.083
-I don't know, 80 pounds?
-Huh?

15:42.117 --> 15:43.419
Like, 36 kilos.

15:43.520 --> 15:46.292
Oh, my God!
That's too much kilos!

15:46.358 --> 15:48.362
Oh, I'm also assigning you
a new partner.

15:48.462 --> 15:50.634
But don't worry, I know
you're nearing retirement

15:50.734 --> 15:52.070
and want a stable situation,

15:52.136 --> 15:55.109
so I'm hooking you up with a guy
named Sergeant Maniac.

15:55.176 --> 15:57.413
How you doing?
I'm a crazy wild card

15:57.480 --> 16:01.021
as indicated by my
only right now timely mullet.

16:01.121 --> 16:04.193
Hmm. You ain't dressed
like a police detective.

16:04.294 --> 16:06.866
Well, I know we're gonna be
running around chasing bad guys,

16:06.967 --> 16:09.304
so I wore
the tightest jeans I own.

16:09.371 --> 16:11.141
Hi-ya! Hi-ya!

16:11.208 --> 16:13.881
Hey, why don't you come on out
to my beachside trailer

16:14.014 --> 16:16.018
to, uh, discuss the case?

16:16.085 --> 16:17.287
Sure. Where is it?

16:17.387 --> 16:20.026
Eh, not in Malibu--
they wouldn't allow it--

16:20.126 --> 16:22.565
but one of those garbage beaches
further north,

16:22.631 --> 16:25.336
way past Moonshadows, which is,
like, the perfect place

16:25.403 --> 16:27.908
to get drunk and tell everybody
who's responsible

16:27.975 --> 16:29.746
for all the world's wars.

16:29.812 --> 16:32.552
♪ ♪

16:32.618 --> 16:36.526
[Cleveland]
I soon realized my new partner
had serious issues.

16:36.593 --> 16:39.799
He didn't care what kind
of dangerous stuff he did.

16:39.866 --> 16:41.603
-[phone rings]
-Hello?

16:41.670 --> 16:44.976
You're calling from
"credit card services"?

16:45.042 --> 16:47.179
Great, I'll tell you
my Social Security number,

16:47.246 --> 16:49.618
and you tell me if it matches
what you have there.

16:49.652 --> 16:51.689
Man is insane.

16:51.756 --> 16:54.862
Okay, and, uh, don't laugh
at my mother's maiden name.

16:54.962 --> 16:56.566
It's kind of a goofy one.

16:56.666 --> 17:00.240
Tinkleman. [laughing] Yeah.
It's like... like pee.

17:00.306 --> 17:02.945
I thought we were gonna
discuss the case.

17:03.045 --> 17:04.849
Right. I'll be ready
in one minute, but first,

17:04.916 --> 17:08.422
I've been asked to make sure
women come see the movie, too.

17:08.523 --> 17:11.227
♪ ♪

17:13.934 --> 17:17.842
[Cleveland]
So my crazy partner and I
set out to solve the case

17:17.908 --> 17:19.712
and began by looking for Leeds,

17:19.778 --> 17:22.049
which was a somewhat popular
mattress store,

17:22.149 --> 17:23.853
where if you said you were
a potential customer,

17:23.920 --> 17:26.726
they'd let you take a nap
in the middle of the day.

17:26.792 --> 17:27.928
-[snoring]
-Sorry, guys.

17:28.028 --> 17:29.732
My manager says
you have to leave.

17:29.799 --> 17:33.172
Leave? But my partner and I
are trying out this queen bed.

17:33.239 --> 17:35.911
-[giggles]
-What are you giggling at?

17:36.011 --> 17:37.982
We're partners
on the police force.

17:38.048 --> 17:40.253
This guy's wearing jeans
with no underwear.

17:40.286 --> 17:42.858
Yeah, you're cops. Sure.

17:42.958 --> 17:45.931
♪ ♪

17:45.998 --> 17:47.802
You guys are no closer
to figuring out

17:47.868 --> 17:50.339
who's responsible for
bringing in all this cocaine.

17:50.406 --> 17:51.843
I got a pretty good idea.

17:51.876 --> 17:54.848
Have you checked Temple
Shalom Yisrael in Brentwood?

17:54.915 --> 17:58.189
It's also where they control
the weather and the Oscars.

17:58.256 --> 18:00.561
That's it.
You guys are off the case.

18:00.627 --> 18:02.631
♪ ♪

18:02.731 --> 18:04.569
[Cleveland]
Since we'd been thrown off
the case,

18:04.635 --> 18:06.973
I thought it'd be nice
to invite my partner over

18:07.073 --> 18:09.277
-for a home-cooked meal.
-Huh.

18:09.377 --> 18:11.014
You don't have a pitcher
of iced tea?

18:11.148 --> 18:12.651
I thought
every Black family dinner

18:12.718 --> 18:14.154
had a pitcher of iced tea.

18:14.254 --> 18:16.325
We do have a picture of Ice-T,

18:16.391 --> 18:18.329
right up there on the wall.

18:18.395 --> 18:19.898
[dispatcher]
Attention, all units, be advised

18:20.032 --> 18:21.736
of a possible drug deal
at the dock.

18:21.803 --> 18:23.138
That's not far from here.

18:23.239 --> 18:25.476
No way.
We were taken off that case.

18:25.544 --> 18:29.117
Yeah, but we can be there before
even the closest patrol car.

18:32.791 --> 18:34.762
♪ ♪

18:46.819 --> 18:49.157
There, look.
Quick, pull over and let me out.

18:49.257 --> 18:51.462
-What?
-I'm gonna run
the rest of the way.

18:51.530 --> 18:53.767
I assure you the car
will be faster.

18:53.834 --> 18:54.769
See you there.

18:54.835 --> 18:56.872
♪ ♪

18:58.442 --> 18:59.477
[grunts]

19:03.687 --> 19:06.525
[panting, grunting]

19:06.592 --> 19:08.295
Been waiting here
for six minutes.

19:08.362 --> 19:11.936
Okay, okay, okay,
so, six-minute mile.

19:12.036 --> 19:13.707
Not bad for jeans
and no underpants.

19:13.773 --> 19:17.246
You got any glovebox Vaseline
in there?

19:19.885 --> 19:22.256
It's the chief. What the hell?

19:23.727 --> 19:25.262
[yells]

19:30.339 --> 19:31.876
The chief has been
the mastermind

19:31.943 --> 19:34.448
of the cocaine cartel all along.

19:34.481 --> 19:37.755
That might explain why
he always calls me at 3:00 a.m.

19:37.821 --> 19:39.792
with screenplay ideas.

19:39.892 --> 19:41.929
[phone ringing]

19:43.331 --> 19:44.969
[grunts] Hello?

19:45.069 --> 19:46.238
[Carter]
Okay, hear me out.

19:46.272 --> 19:48.342
It's Die Hard,
but in a building.

19:48.409 --> 19:50.747
Die Hard is in a building.

19:50.814 --> 19:53.185
Hmm, I don't know.
Here, listen to me watch it,

19:53.251 --> 19:54.487
and we'll find out.

19:54.621 --> 19:57.861
[20th Century Fox fanfare
playing over phone]

20:02.136 --> 20:04.273
[both grunt]

20:11.488 --> 20:14.061
Give it up.
You guys can't arrest me anyway.

20:14.127 --> 20:17.267
I have diplomatic immunity.

20:17.367 --> 20:20.239
-You do?
-On what basis?

20:20.306 --> 20:22.376
Yeah, I'm a citizen
of Margaritaville.

20:22.410 --> 20:25.249
I even have this hat from
a recent vacation to prove it.

20:25.316 --> 20:27.655
[growls] Too bad.

20:27.755 --> 20:31.996
Your diplomatic immunity's
just been revoked.

20:32.063 --> 20:33.498
[groans]

20:35.637 --> 20:37.875
The officer's actions,
while illegal,

20:37.942 --> 20:41.549
were justified by a snappy line.
Movie over.

20:41.649 --> 20:44.420
[ominous synth music playing]

20:44.487 --> 20:46.892
[Quagmire]
I was also a producer
on this project.